    </div>
    @if (snapshot is not null)
    {
        @if (snapshots.FirstOrDefault(item => item.Id == snapshot)?.Tags.Contains("lms-full-system") == true)
        {
            <details class="backup-recovery-guide"><summary><strong>Full-system / bare-metal recovery</strong></summary>
                <ol><li>Before failure, restore the boot-recovery ISO from this snapshot to a private folder and keep boot media offline.</li><li>Boot that ISO on the replacement machine. Connect the backup storage; if password protected, keep the password independently of LMS.</li><li>Run <code>rear recover</code> at its console. Enter the repository path; enter its password privately, or press Enter for password-free storage. The ISO finds its matching completed backup and checks its data before any disk changes. Review the proposed target disks carefully before approving recreation.</li><li>Check Linux boot, LMS login, saved credentials and required workloads. Record the test against this plan. See FULL-SYSTEM-RECOVERY.txt in the encrypted snapshot.</li></ol>
